lesson: 86
title: When the remainder needs one more
stars: 0
explain: When everyone or everything must fit, the ones left over still need a place, so we need one more group.
explain: 26 children in vans of 6: 26 ÷ 6 = 4 vans with 2 children left over, so 5 vans are needed.
explain: Divide, and if there is a remainder, add one.
vars: a=name t=thing n=10..80 k=3..9
need: n % k != 0
need: n > k
let: q = (n - n % k) / k
answer: q + 1
exercise: {n} children go on a trip. Each van carries {k} children. How many vans are needed?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. Each box holds {k} {t}. How many boxes does {a} need to pack all the {t}?
exercise: {n} people want to cross the river. The boat takes {k} people at a time. How many trips must the boat make?
exercise: A table seats {k} guests. How many tables are needed for {n} guests?
exercise: {a} must read {n} pages and reads {k} pages a day. How many days does {a} need to finish?
exercise: {n} students go camping. Each tent sleeps {k} students. How many tents are needed?
test: How many cars are needed to take {n} players to a game if one car fits {k} players?
test: Every shelf holds {k} books. What is the smallest number of shelves that holds {n} books?
test: {a} wants to put all {n} {t} into bags of {k}. How many bags must {a.he} use, even if one is not full?
test: A rowing boat has {k} seats. How many boats does a school need so that {n} pupils all have a seat?
exercise: How many vans are needed to carry {n} children if every van holds {k}?
exercise: {a} packs {n} {t} into boxes that hold {k} each. How many boxes does {a.he} need so that no {t} are left out?
exercise: A minibus in Wales takes {k} people. How many minibuses are needed for {n} people?
exercise: {n} campers in Oregon sleep in tents for {k} campers each. How many tents do they need?
exercise: {a} has {n} photos, and an album page holds {k}. How many pages does {a} need for all the photos?
exercise: A lift in a London hotel carries {k} people at a time. {n} people must go up. What is the least number of trips the lift must make?
exercise: {a} reads {k} pages each night, and the book has {n} pages. How many nights will it take {a.him} to finish the book?
exercise: {n} guests come to a party in Auckland, and each table seats {k}. How many tables are needed so every guest has a seat?
test: Cards come in packs of {k}. {a} needs {n} cards. How many packs must {a.he} buy?
test: What is the least number of boats, each holding {k} people, that can carry {n} people across a lake in Ontario?
test: A school in Cork sends {n} pupils to a match in cars that take {k} pupils each. How many cars does it need?
test: {n} muffins must go into boxes of {k}. How many boxes are needed to hold every muffin?
test: {a} can carry {k} {t} on one trip. How many trips does {a.he} make to move {n} {t}?
test: A ride in Florida takes {k} children at a time. How many rides are needed so all {n} children get a turn?
