exam: It is given that {n} children are to be conveyed by vans, each having a capacity of {k} children. Determine the minimum number of vans required to convey all the children.
exam: Ascertain the least number of boxes, each accommodating {k.words} {t}, that is sufficient to contain {n.words} {t}.
exam: Whereas {a} is in possession of {n} {t} and each container holds no more than {k}, state the minimum number of containers required to pack the entirety of the {t}.
exam: Compute the smallest number of tables, each seating {k} persons, necessary to seat {n} guests.
exercise: Grandad passed away and left {n} old records. {a} packs them into boxes that hold {k} each. How many boxes does {a} need to pack every record?
exercise: The firm is "downsizing", so {n} desks have to go. A van takes {k} desks a trip. How many trips are needed to move all the desks?
test: nan's dog crossed the rainbow bridge, poor thing. {n} tins of his food left, a bag takes {k}. how many bags to shift the bloody lot
